# 🧾 ADR Reporting & Documentation (VirtualWorkLab Task 2)

## 📘 Overview
This project simulates a **pharmacovigilance ADR reporting system** used in healthcare and pharmaceutical industries.  
It is part of the **VirtualWorkLab Task 2** — *ADR Reporting & Documentation*.

The goal is to complete a structured ADR reporting form based on a given case scenario, documenting suspected adverse drug reactions (ADRs) accurately.

---

## 🧠 Features
- Patient Information entry (Name, Age, Gender)
- Suspected Medicine details (Name, Dose, Start Date)
- Adverse Reaction documentation (Description, Date of Recovery, Seriousness)
- Reporter Information (Name, Contact)
- Additional Notes section for clinical observations

---

## 🧩 Technologies Used
- HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript  
- Python (optional backend for data handling)  
- Bootstrap for responsive UI  

